1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:11,000
Start with the attachment numbers. The clinic receipt matches the intake log they recovered. The whole file got in.

2
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,130
This receipt says complete.

3
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:25,260
Complete at intake. Check the numbers before you write that.

4
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:28,770
So someone just ignored it?

5
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,180
Which list are you looking at?

6
00:00:36,830 --> 00:00:39,160
The one they received.

7
00:00:39,810 --> 00:00:45,290
That's the customer intake list. Put it beside this one.

8
00:00:48,800 --> 00:01:01,620
Wait. This is what the doctor saw. The attachment never reached the medical review queue. He opened the page and signed. It wasn't there.

9
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,660
So neither record was fake.

10
00:01:08,310 --> 00:01:12,220
Could this just be a later copy?

11
00:01:12,870 --> 00:01:18,350
Check the date and case number. Same case, same review.

12
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:32,050
Here's their reply to her quality report. Months earlier. They'd been told about the gap. But these later denial letters still say they considered everything.

13
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:36,080
Did they say they'd fix it?

14
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:49,800
They said they'd received my report. That's what that reply proves.

15
00:01:50,450 --> 00:01:57,500
I wrote the report. I also signed those later forms. You need both.

16
00:01:58,150 --> 00:01:59,960
After that reply?

17
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:01,670
Yes.

18
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:14,950
Tomorrow: Ellie's files. The originals. No edits. You need to see what they put this family through.

19
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:18,460
Is he talking about me?

20
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:28,800
Yes. I'll tell them to stop. Should I put it away?

21
00:02:29,450 --> 00:02:34,410
After you tell them. And don't show my whale.

22
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:49,480
Use what you've checked. Keep her name out. No treatment photos. I agreed to a review, not this.

23
00:02:55,800 --> 00:03:01,280
Mara wants the records taken down. Kevin's working on it.

24
00:03:01,930 --> 00:03:04,790
Which ones post for me?

25
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:24,980
These two handle my posts. Tell them to take her records down. Don't send them any more copies.

26
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:28,340
The third one isn't mine.

27
00:03:28,990 --> 00:03:34,190
Then don't mark it. Kevin can send a separate request.

28
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:43,380
I'll ask. But the copies are out there. And Blake may just say no.

29
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:51,080
Ask anyway. And put that away. She doesn't need a statement from me.

30
00:03:55,800 --> 00:04:00,760
These are your quotes. Check the last line too.

31
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:07,000
It's accurate. You can use my name.

32
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:19,950
My lawyer wants that line about signing cut. Leave it in. Just take the patient numbers off.

33
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:31,850
The patient files stay with Kevin. The download is just the redacted findings.

34
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:38,500
Send me the link. Interview's tomorrow. I'll have to explain this.

35
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:48,280
Do you want me to hold the link until after?

36
00:04:48,930 --> 00:04:58,080
No. Send it when it's up. I don't want to walk in pretending they haven't read it.
